
"smart_sources:ServiceNowOfficialDocs/support-and-troubleshooting/performance/KB0790981 - Existing archive rule on taskcmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent taskcmdb table.md": {"path":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/support-and-troubleshooting/performance/KB0790981 - Existing archive rule on taskcmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent taskcmdb table.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"arrnzd","at":1784561349683},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1783354428475,"size":3624,"at":1784561349684,"hash":"arrnzd"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,11],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table":[13,85],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#Issue":[17,18],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#**For Cmdb table issue example:**":[19,28],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#**For Cmdb table issue example:**#**1) We want to implement archiving for the cmdb tables and its children tables.**":[21,22],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#**For Cmdb table issue example:**#**2) We originally had a rule that worked at the cmdb\\_ci table at a high level.**":[23,24],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#**For Cmdb table issue example:**#**3) We archived Computers and Personal Computers, but then if I tried to setup an archive for CMDB\\_CI the table was not shown, in order to archive it.**":[25,26],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#**For Cmdb table issue example:**#**4) Therefore, we modified the existing archive rule with one at the lowest level of that chain of extended tables to be CMDB\\_CI\\_PC\\_Hardware then tried to create a new rule for its parent table CMDB\\_CI\\_Computer, it was still not shown.**":[27,28],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#**For Task table issue example:**":[29,38],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#**For Task table issue example:**#**1) We want to implement archiving for the task tables and its children tables.**":[31,32],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#**For Task table issue example:**#**2) We originally had a rule that worked at the task table at a high level.**":[33,34],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#**For Task table issue example:**#**3) We archived children tables from the task table, but then if I tried to setup an archive for the task table, the table was greyed out that did not allow us to select it in order to archive it.**":[35,36],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#**For Task table issue example:**#**4) We also have archived children tables from the task table where it does not allow us to create archive rules for 2nd layer children tables of 1st layer children tables from the task table.**":[37,38],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#Release":[39,42],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#Release#**This applies to all environments**":[41,42],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#Cause":[43,55],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#Cause#**1) We found out that the reason why you can't select the parent task or parent cmdb table or 2nd layer children tables from 1st layer children tables of task or children tables from cmdb is because unfortunately our system is not designed to create multiple archive rules per hierarchy (vertically) in any table that has extended tables (children tables).**":[45,46],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#Cause#**2) This is a known issue documented on PRB713693**":[47,55],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#Cause#**2) This is a known issue documented on PRB713693**#{1}":[49,55],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#Resolution":[56,85],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#Resolution#**WARNING****:** **This approach will work in respects to archiving, but will not make Archive Destroy fully work for children cmdb or task archive tables due to PRB1764668.**":[58,59],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#Resolution#**The best solution I have for you to be able to archive per hierarchy in one archive rule is the following:**":[60,85],"##Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table#Resolution#**The best solution I have for you to be able to archive per hierarchy in one archive rule is the following:**#{1}":[62,85]},"outlinks":[],"metadata":{"title":"Existing archive rule on task/cmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent task/cmdb table","aliases":["KB0790981"],"tags":["#servicenow","#support-kb"],"source_url":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=KB0790981","kb_number":"KB0790981","last_modified":"2024-08-05"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},"smart_blocks:ServiceNowOfficialDocs/support-and-troubleshooting/performance/KB0790981 - Existing archive rule on taskcmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent taskcmdb table.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"mtrupa","at":1784561349683},"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/support-and-troubleshooting/performance/KB0790981 - Existing archive rule on taskcmdb child table prevents creation of new archive rule in parent taskcmdb table.md#---frontmatter---","lines":[1,11],"size":324,"outlinks":[],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
